L=['# Removing expanded response storage: real memory saving, expensive recomputation','', '**Completed decision:** the exact no-W/no-M representation works and preserves the original-equation acceptance contract, but is a memory–compute tradeoff, not a faster solver. Three fresh sequential workers completed the single fixed N128, k=0 comparison. No other mode, tolerance, leaf size or compression rank was tried.','', '## State and unchanged model','', 'The previous operator-first construction keeps actual stored frequencies, all 12 angular channels, full anisotropic phase, the original min/gather background, and the nonzero grazing velocities. It compresses only the known scalar normal derivative while preserving skew-Hermitian structure. This follow-up changes only the inverse-factor storage/evaluation of the same Gtilde. Cached and recomputing derivative matrices have the same byte hash: `'+analysis['unchanged_Dtilde_sha256']+'`.','', f"The unchanged exact-arithmetic model bound is ||I-G Gtilde^-1|| <= q={q:.9g}. The same original residual target 1e-10 and max 3 repairs apply. Floating implementations have additional per-input E=I-Gtilde Bhat; the earlier q+(1+q)||E|| accounting remains necessary. No uniform floating or interval certificate is claimed. No physical source, held-out dataset, training, full dense Green inverse or outer heterogeneous-RTE solve was used.",'', '## Exact construction without stored W or M','', 'For Gtilde=[[A,U_L V_R*],[U_R V_L*,B]], define S=I-(V_L*A^-1 U_L)(V_R*B^-1 U_R). Store only pivoted leaf factors and S LU. U and V actions retain the scalar spatial factors and actual angular diagonal, without keeping their angular-expanded tensors. For each RHS:','', '    yR = B^-1 qR','    zL = A^-1 (qL - U_L V_R* yR)','    a  = S^-1 V_L* zL','    tR = B^-1 U_R a','    xR = yR - tR','    xL = zL + A^-1 U_L V_R* tR','', 'Substitution into the two block equations proves the identity. This removes W_L,W_R,M_L,M_R from persistent storage. It does NOT remove the Schur LU. To avoid claiming a low persistent footprint after a high-memory constructor, each S was constructed in fixed 12-column panels, one scalar interface coordinate times all angles, using child solves. The expanded W/M matrices were never constructed then freed. Every streamed child solve is paid in setup.','', 'This evaluation circuit makes two left and two right child solves. Its recurrence is T(n)=4T(n/2)+local work, versus two child solves plus cached W/M contractions. With the fixed four-level tree, one application makes 256 leaf visits rather than 16. This is a property of this circuit, not a universal lower bound on every structured solver, nor a prediction of 16x total arithmetic or wall time. Removing cached contractions offsets some additional work.','', 'The new small recursive algebra unit passed against both a dense solve and the cached factor. On the real object, independently instrumented calls measured exactly 31/341 node visits and 16/256 leaf visits for cached/recomputing respectively. Instrumentation was removed for all reported application timings.','', '## Accuracy and matched cost','', 'Each process paid its own physical setup and method-specific setup. Angular-band did not pay a derivative tree it does not use. Three checked applications of the same five input columns (three normalized complex random, exact zero, 1e-200 nonzero) were retained, including the first call. No warmup result was removed. A small accepted cached reference was written/read only after construction for equality checks; this cost is recorded.','', '| Method | Factor MB | Factor s | Physical + used tree + factor s | Three checked applications, s | Mean s | Max original residual |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|']
