L+=['', f"All nine checked applications passed, all with one original-G repair, including zero/tiny handling. Recomputing differs from the accepted cached solution by at most {r1['max_relative_to_cached']:.6g}. Its raw Gtilde solve residual reached {max(D['recompute']['raw_approximate_relative']):.6g}, versus {max(D['cached']['raw_approximate_relative']):.6g} cached; this extra floating error was not assumed away.",'', f"Persistent tensor storage is {r1['factor_bytes']/r0['factor_bytes']:.4f}x cached and {r1['factor_bytes']/r2['factor_bytes']:.4f}x angular-band. The exact reduction removes 17,989,632 W bytes and 9,331,200 M bytes; the recomputing action additionally retains the 192-byte actual direction backing storage. The remaining representation still includes 4,665,600 bytes of expanded Schur LU, 2,359,296 leaf LU bytes, 12,912 pivot bytes and 141,312 scalar-tree bytes.",'', f"Observed streamed factor setup was {analysis['recompute_vs_cached_factor_time_ratio']:.3f}x cached and {analysis['recompute_vs_angular_factor_time_ratio']:.3f}x angular-band. Across all three applications, mean time was {analysis['recompute_vs_cached_application_mean_ratio']:.3f}x cached and {analysis['recompute_vs_angular_application_mean_ratio']:.3f}x angular-band. These are this single-object diagnostic's observations, not a general timing theorem or a full-RTE throughput result. A tighter memory limit could make the tradeoff useful; that is not the present speed objective.",'', '## Resident memory, including setup workspace','', '| Method | Factor-phase process high-water MiB | Application-phase high-water MiB | Complete external process peak MiB |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in rows:L.append(f"| {r['method']} | {r['factor_phase_peak_RSS_bytes']/2**20:.3f} | {r['application_phase_peak_RSS_bytes']/2**20:.3f} | {r['external_full_process_peak_RSS_bytes']/2**20:.3f} |")
L+=['', 'Logical factor bytes and whole-process RSS are different measurements. All three workers started separately, so no method carries another factor in its reported footprint. RSS includes PyTorch/runtime, original operator, buffers and allocator history. The cached process later performs additional structure diagnostics, so its final process peak is not the like-for-like factor peak. The external receipt also covers final serialization/shutdown after the last internal sample. The memory saving is real in both stored tensors and measured process footprint, but is much smaller in full-process percentage than the factor ratio.','', '## Why two easy ways to remove Schur storage are not established','', '**1. Primitive angular banding is not closed under inversion.** In the actual stored data, the 12 entries of Omega=diag(omega_n) are distinct (minimum separation '+f"{st['minimum_normal_separation']:.6g}), and every phase entry is nonzero (minimum {st['minimum_absolute_phase_entry']:.6g}). Polynomial interpolation in Omega produces each coordinate projector E_ii. Then E_ii K E_jj / K_ij=E_ij. Hence the algebra generated by Omega and K is all 12-by-12 matrices. A small fixed exact angular algebra cannot be inferred from the original few Kronecker terms or near-banded angular Fourier representation.",'', 'This theorem does not prove that the particular current W/S tensors need full approximate separation rank. The exact distinctness partly comes from tiny stored rounding differences. Any approximation exploiting near symmetry is a different preconditioner and needs an added original-A0-weighted defect bound. Existing angular-band already exploits primitive angular structure before elimination; it does not license silently truncating inverse-response factors.','', '| Root factor object in angular Fourier coordinates | Frobenius fraction outside cyclic nearest-angular band |','|---|---:|']
