L+=['', 'These nonzero off-band measurements are diagnostic, not an original-weighted certificate for any truncated inverse. No band-truncated W/S solver was run.','', '**2. A matrix-free Schur inverse needs a new convergence argument.** Removing S LU leaves S-vector actions, each requiring two child inverse actions. On the existing 396-dimensional root, ||S||F='+f"{st['root_S_F_norm']:.9g}; therefore by the triangle inequality and ||X||F<=sqrt(R)||X||2,",'', '    ||I-S||2 >= (||S||F-sqrt(R))/sqrt(R) = '+f"{st['identity_Neumann_2norm_lower_bound']:.9g} > 1.",'', 'Thus taking I as an inverse and invoking a Euclidean operator-norm-contractive Neumann argument is unavailable. This is not proof that the spectral radius is >1, and does not rule out another interface preconditioner. Original-G accretivity alone is insufficient: rescaling equivalent interface coordinates can change Euclidean Schur conditioning without changing G. No matrix-free interface iteration was launched.','', '## What the nested-basis escape would actually require','', 'A nested HSS/ULV elimination is a materially different representation that could avoid this recomputation circuit. It cannot simply reuse the old sibling ranks. An exact nested basis must span restrictions of ancestor interface bases as well as its sibling interaction. The four fixed 32-cell restrictions were checked, without a rank/tolerance search:','', '| Quarter | Inherited numerical rank | Smallest inherited singular value | Combined inherited+sibling numerical rank | Smallest combined singular value |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
