L+=['', 'All are numerically full row rank under the recorded standard floating-point rank threshold. The conditional algebraic statement is simple: a rank-32 inherited map on 32 cells needs 32 interface directions for exact representation, so there are no redundant normal directions to eliminate at that node. The numerical observation is not an exact-rational rank certificate and not a theorem that approximate nesting is impossible. Smaller nested interfaces would require recompressing the inherited+local spaces and charging that new error to the original-A0 bound; the old rank14/8 sibling counts and q cannot just be reused.','', 'Classical nested-factor methods are described in [Chandrasekaran, Gu and Pals, A Fast ULV Decomposition Solver for Hierarchically Semiseparable Representations](https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/S0895479803436652). That is distinct from Hermitian/skew-Hermitian splitting, also called HSS in this repository. Their small-rank premise and cost claims have not been established for this actual RTE derivative/factor.','', '## Complete numerical process accounting','', '| Worker | Wall s | User s | Sys s | External peak RSS KiB | Exit |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
